WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.500
- I heard that you said "Rocky"

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.150
couldn't have existed without

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.730
Carl Weathers, right?
- No, I'm, you know, it-

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.260
first of all, Rocky's a, oh, I know.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.280
- [Kelly] Look at that
photo, it's so iconic, wow.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.200
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.603
- Yeah, he was amaze-

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.270
I couldn't find anyone to play the part.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.100
No one had all the tools.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.470
Either the voice was too high or their,

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.570
they weren't big enough or
they weren't athletic enough.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.410
It's really hard to find
everything in a person.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:28.080
So it was about eight o'clock at night

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.170
and the guy I wanted, so then he quit

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.350
because he wants to go in
a bicycle race competition.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.640
I went, "Really?"

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:38.220
So obviously he was not a serious actor.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.660
He was a physical type.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.870
So I'm sitting there and at
8:30, this fellow comes in

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.600
and he's mad, like, "What am I here for?"

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.400
I mean, 'cause no one gets a-

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.620
like you don't have an
audition at 8:30 at night.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.690
You're, like, at the bottom of the barrel,

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.523
you know what I mean?
- Oh.

00:00:52.523 --> 00:00:53.356
- You know what I mean, it's-
- I didn't-

00:00:53.356 --> 00:00:54.330
- Like noon, lunch.
- Know that, oh okay.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.350
It's, like, 8:30.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.910
- Oh.
- So he comes in,

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.580
they pulled him off a
plane going to Oakland.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.657
So he's coming and he's fired up.

00:01:01.657 --> 00:01:03.270
"All right, what do I do?"

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.567
I go, "Voice good.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:05.730
"Voice is good.
(audience and Kelly laughs)

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:06.563
Good, check that."

00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:08.940
He goes, and he takes his jacket off,

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.850
shoulders forever,
(audience chuckles)

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:11.683
- [Kelly] Check.

00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:14.010
- Check, and then he looked,

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.250
I went, "Good looking." you know, nice.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.560
I didn't expect that, you
know, 'cause he is a boxer.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.640
- Tough.
- And then we start,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.040
and tough, then we started to
get up and I'm telling you,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.690
and he goes, "Pow, pow, pow."

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.464
I go (censored) damn,

00:01:26.464 --> 00:01:27.297
and I go, "It's like
(audience and Kelly laughs)

00:01:27.297 --> 00:01:28.680
a woodpecker hit me."

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.640
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.840
- Check.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:31.833
And then he goes,

00:01:32.677 --> 00:01:37.380
"I would've done better if you
at least hired a real actor

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.970
instead of, what do you do,

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.650
what's this guy do, work in the office?"

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.311
I go, "No, he's Rocky." he went,

00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:44.340
(audience moans)
"All right, how you

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.180
doing Rocky?" he's like,
(audience and Kelly laughs)

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.794
there was, and I go-

00:01:47.794 --> 00:01:50.002
- This guy.
- "Arrogant, got it."

00:01:50.002 --> 00:01:51.180
(audience laughs)

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.044
- But you need him-
- This guy that works

00:01:52.044 --> 00:01:52.877
in the office.
- You know what I mean.

00:01:52.877 --> 00:01:53.970
I wanted that-
- Yeah.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.080
- I wanted him to have this,

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.550
like Muhammad Ali.
- (sighs) Ah.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.930
- But he had it all, he had charm,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.580
he had this, he had heart, he had soul.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:03.060
So I was stunned when it
happened, I was, like, crushed.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:04.770
I didn't think he would ever die.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.450
You know, he is like superman.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:11.340
Yeah, so I look back now with
fond, fond, fond memories.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.360
'Cause it's never gonna happen.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.250
You know what happens, you
have those seminal moments,

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.541
those crossroads, and it's like-

00:02:15.541 --> 00:02:16.560
- And certain Chemistry

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.730
on certain things.
- Yeah, it's just,

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.800
it's impossible to duplicate.

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.633
You know, it's like if-
- Yeah I know.

00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:22.020
- They take a group,

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.520
and let's say the Rolling Stones, right.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.650
You take Mick Jagger out, it's over.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.600
You take Mick Jagger, the solo.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.770
I don't think it works either.

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.180
There's something about-
- They fit.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:33.450
- That combination that was so unique

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.250
that you can't mess with it.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.150
- Yeah.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.130
- And I think that happened with Rocky.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:39.330
Everybody in it was, like,

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.280
sort of born to play the part.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.133
- Yeah.
- Hey.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.170
- [Kelly] I love it, and when it works out

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.430
like that, that's why it's so successful.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.903
- Yeah, it is, it is.

